// Two reflexivities whose points no rule relates are not one path: the twin
// of the model's `peak_is_here` (the HoTT book's § 1.12, `refl`, under
// judgmental equality). `S(x)` and `P(x)` share no normal form under the
// integers' cancellations, so `here(P(x))` is no path from `S(x)` to `S(x)`.

// The integers, presented by their two cancellations.
import "../../model/identity/circle-base.gandr";

/// The reflexivity at a successor beside the reflexivity at a predecessor,
/// refused: no rule relates `P(x)` to `S(x)` (#1723).
@[ refuses("EndpointMismatch") ]
def peak_apart(x : Int) -> Path(Path(Int, S(x), S(x)), here(S(x)), here(P(x))) {
  here(here(S(x)))
}
